Pomelo: phone-usable desktop-Android extensions.

Rebased onto Chromium 158.0.8127.43 from danosito/afterbird patches/m151
(BSD-3-Clause, https://github.com/danosito/afterbird):

- Manifest V2 stays installable (manifest_v2_util::IsExtensionAffected).
- browser_action and page_action schemas stay bundled when enable_extensions
  is false, which is the desktop-Android configuration.
- The extensions app-menu item opens chrome://extensions on a phone, where
  ExtensionsToolbarCoordinator is null.
- Unpacked extensions, including a sideloaded CRX that is installed as
  unpacked, are not gated on the developer-mode pref.
- The Chrome Web Store is loaded with a desktop user agent so its install
  button is shown.

